# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manuscript prose — NOT part of this repository.
#
# The line drawn here is between the *manuscript* and the *evidence*. The
# manuscript — drafts, revision reports, handoff bundles — is written elsewhere
# and stays there. The evidence layer that backs its numbers is published:
# without the study dataset, the reproduction pipeline, the regenerated audit
# outputs and the methodology notes, no reader can check a single validation
# figure, which is the whole point of releasing the tool openly.
#
# So: `src/algametrix/paper/`, `data/studies/`, `reproduce.py`,
# `tests/test_paper_*.py`, `results/`, `figures/`, `scripts/fetch_indices.py`
# and the three methodology notes in `docs/` are all tracked deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The assembled Supplementary Information bundle. Its generator
# (src/algametrix/paper/supplementary.py) and every input it embeds are tracked;
# the bundle itself is not, because it is a byte-for-byte restatement of
# results/ and docs/ and would double the repository's text for no added
# checkability. `python reproduce.py --only supplementary` rebuilds it.
/supplementary/

# Manuscript drafts, revision reports and handoff bundles
/paper_handoff/
/revision_handoff/
/revision_handoff_r2/
/handoff_zip/
/jie_handoff/
/REVISION_REPORT.md
/00_START_HERE.md
*.zip

# Tooling that assembles the private manuscript bundle; the rest of scripts/
# is part of the published pipeline.
/scripts/make_handoff.py
